  "description": "<p>The default triples from Fedora 5.1.0 for a binary are</p>\n\n<p>&lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1</a>&gt;<br/>\n    rdf:type fedora:Binary ;<br/>\n    rdf:type fedora:Resource ;<br/>\n    fedora:lastModifiedBy \"bypassAdmin\" ;<br/>\n    premis:hasSize \"17\"^^&lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#long</a>&gt; ;<br/>\n    ebucore:hasMimeType \"text/plain\" ;<br/>\n    fedora:createdBy \"bypassAdmin\" ;<br/>\n    fedora:created \"2020-04-02T16:21:49.406Z\"^^&lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime</a>&gt; ;<br/>\n    fedora:lastModified \"2020-04-02T16:21:49.406Z\"^^&lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime</a>&gt; ;<br/>\n    premis:hasMessageDigest &lt;urn:sha1:482cb0cfcbed6740a2bcb659c9ccc22a4d27b369&gt; ;<br/>\n    ebucore:filename \"\" ;<br/>\n    rdf:type ldp:NonRDFSource ;<br/>\n    iana:describedby &lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1/fcr:metadata\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1/fcr:metadata</a>&gt; ;<br/>\n    fedora:hasFixityService &lt;<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1/fcr:fixity\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/binary1/fcr:fixity</a>&gt; .</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Some of these triples probably are not needed or can be a different syntax.</p>\n\n<p>For example <tt>iana:describedby</tt> is now a header and not needed. Also in Fedora 5 we had to restrict the updating of the <tt>ebucore:hasMimetype</tt> as it was necessary to allow us to serve the binary (<a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2520).\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2520).</a> I would recommend that we store the incoming mimetype under a server managed property so user RDF changes don't need to be vetted and we can still serve the binary.</p>",
